  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The program gate now judges the operations of each mount with no machine against the limits of the default machine file (`3axis-vmc.mch`). The post writes these operations with that file, so the gate reads the same values.\n- The gate judges two limits: the spindle speed range and the feed rate of each linear axis. These are the same checks that a mounted machine gets, in the same words.\n- The refusal names the default machine, each operation and each limit. It tells the user to mount a machine on the setup or to change the operation.\n- `posting::default_limits` reads the limits from the default file. The file uses the post grammar (`kinematics.static`), so `parse_mch` cannot read it. A zero, negative or absent number is unstated and checks nothing.\n- If the default file does not read, the gate refuses by the file name and names the setups (#2319).\n- A mounted machine is judged by its own file only, as before. The status line machine vote does not change.\n- The new code is in `crates/app/src/posting_default_machine.rs`. `posting_mounts.rs` gets one call. `posting.rs` changes one `pub use` line and does not grow.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2321-default-machine-limits.md`.\n\n## Readings on the code before the fix\n\n- An operation at 7000 mm/min posted with no refusal. The default X/Y rate is 5000 mm/min.\n- An operation at 15000 rpm was refused only by the engine warning `spindle rpm over machine maximum`. That text names no operation and no limit. The gate now refuses it first, by name.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/default_machine_limits.rs`:\n- `no_mounted_machine_is_refused_above_the_default_spindle_maximum` (red before the fix)\n- `no_mounted_machine_is_refused_above_the_default_feed_rate` (red before the fix: the program posted)\n- `only_the_mount_with_no_machine_is_judged_against_the_default` (red before the fix)\n- `no_mounted_machine_within_the_default_limits_posts`\n- `a_mounted_machine_is_judged_by_its_own_file_only` (a mounted machine with no stated limits posts 15000 rpm and 7000 mm/min, as before)\n- `the_default_limits_are_read_from_the_post_grammar`\n\nRed proof: with the gate clause removed, the three marked tests fail. The other three pass. `default_machine_missing` (9 tests, #2319) passes.\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick`, 810 steps, 0 failed, clippy clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI. The status line vote is not changed.\n- Pose and rotary laws for the default machine. The default file states no rotaries, but this change adds no pose check for documents with no machine (see the decision file).\n- Release-tier heavy lanes.\n\nChangelog: A document with no mounted machine is now refused when an operation exceeds the default machine's spindle speed or feed rate; the refusal names the operation and the limit.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2321\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
